      "type": "mcq_multi",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "If the slope of the parabola $y = ax^2 + bx + c$ at $(2, 3)$ is 5 and the x-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola is 3, then which of the following is/are true?"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "$a = -5/2$"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "$b = 15$"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "$c = -17$"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The parabola opens downwards."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "correct_answers": [
        0,
        3
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Slope $y' = 2ax + b$. At $x = 2$, $4a + b = 5$. Vertex at $x = 3 \\implies -b/(2a) = 3 \\implies b = -6a$. Then $4a - 6a = 5 \\implies -2a = 5 \\implies a = -5/2$. Since $a < 0$, it opens downwards."
        }
      ]
    },
